    "title": "Michigan House rejects plan to change university board selection process - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Boldrey ,\n7 hours ago LANSING, MI — A resolution that would have changed how university boards are selected at three major Michigan universities was stopped in its tracks Wednesday. House Joint Resolution U, which required two-thirds support in the House and Senate to pass, was shot down 54 to 52 in the State House on Wednesday, June 3. Only one Democrat, former House Speaker Joe Tate, voted in favor of it. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
